{"name":"Vanilla Wafer","hex":"#f3ead2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vanilla wafer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A white person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanilla_wafer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wafer","blocks":[{"text":"A wafer is a crisp, often sweet, very thin, flat, light biscuit, often used to decorate ice cream, and also used as a garnish on some sweet dishes. They frequently have a waffle surface pattern but may also be patterned with insignia of the food's manufacturer or may be patternless. Some chocolate bars, such as Kit Kat and Toffee Crisp, are wafers with chocolate in and around them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Akbar_Mashti.JPG/330px-Akbar_Mashti.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wafer"},{"title":"Vanilla","blocks":[{"text":"Vanilla is a spice derived from orchids of the genus Vanilla, primarily obtained from the seed pods of the flat-leaved Mexican and Central American vanilla (V. planifolia)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg/330px-Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla"},{"title":"Vanilla (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color vanilla is a rich tint of off-white as well as a medium pale tint of yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Vanilla_planifolia_1.jpg/330px-Vanilla_planifolia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Karlsbader-Oblate.jpg/500px-Karlsbader-Oblate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia